Category 12,  Topic 2
Message 8         Wed Sep 09, 1987
S.W.SQUIRES [scott]          at 04:02 EDT
          
( MacForth vs Mach2 ) Choosing a Forth is dependent upon what you want out of
it.  Both MacForth and Mach2 are good Forths for the Macintosh ( better than
the Forths I've seen on most machines ).  Each has its own approach, good and
bad depending on what you want.
  Mach2  advantages-
     speed
     same names as Mac Toolbox ( easier to port other Mac programs )
     standard 68000 assembler
     almost Forth-83

  MacForth advantages-
     more complete and powerful development system
     complete libraries  ( higher level starting point )
     source code for all extensions
     no need to have to learn 68000 assembler
     no need to have a copy of Inside Macintosh next to you at all times

All in all both are good packages.  You'll have to decide which is best for
your needs.  I've chosen MacForth so I can develop faster but if I needed to
port from other Mac languages I'd choose Mach2.
  There are a couple of reviews in the file directory but these are somewhat
dated.      -scott

( With each new version both seem to add ideas from the other so some of the
differences are becoming less. )
