Category 12,  Topic 2
Message 11        Wed Sep 09, 1987
W.ASKEY                      at 21:23 PDT
          
John -- Ouch, I should be sentenced to two days of programming in BASIC.  I
ran a LEAVE test in MacFORTH Plus and it DOES use the FORTH-83 LEAVE, my
"problem" was that I originally referenced the MacFORTH Plus glossary which
describes the 79 LEAVE.  I hadn't talked about the MacFORTH LOOP's before,
they are like the 83  standard except that they completely skip the loop body
if the  initial index and limit equal one another (they thus act like a ?DO, I
really prefer MacFORTH's handling of that one).  So, with all "those"   issues
resolved, I'm going to retire myself from the product debate -- satisfied that
we Macintosh users have two very good Forth products in MacFORTH Plus and
MACH2. -- Waymen 
